From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0004/0004] miningNpcOperations: keep a fleet actor the store still owns

The mining fleet record dropped any actor whose runtime controller was not in
the in-memory registry. That registry is rebuilt when a scene is torn down,
while the persisted native controller row survives, so a durable miner or
hauler disappeared from its fleet with no destruction at all: the prune
forensics reported storedEntity=true storedController=true for every removed
actor, the fleet reported miners=0 while the ships were still alive, and the
haul leg never started. A destroyed NPC is removed from the store, so real
losses still prune normally.

Upstream base: c3ea396b6761a0ed3e71ad5b8dd7507f9ae6d69f
Local overlay: integration/* is NOT part of this patch series.
---
--- a/server/src/services/mining/miningNpcOperations.js
+++ b/server/src/services/mining/miningNpcOperations.js
@@ -1561,20 +1561,33 @@ function getMiningFleetsForSystem(systemID) {
       fleets.push(fleetRecord);
     }
   }
   return fleets;
 }
 
+// A durable native NPC owns its hull through the persisted controller row, not
+// through the in-memory registry: the registry is rebuilt whenever a scene is
+// torn down, while the row survives. Dropping such an actor from the fleet
+// silently removes a live ship and the fleet mines nothing forever. Keep it
+// while the store still owns it; a destroyed NPC is removed from the store, so
+// real losses still prune normally.
+function isRetainedFleetActor(entityID) {
+  if (npcService.getControllerByEntityID(entityID)) {
+    return true;
+  }
+  return Boolean(nativeNpcStore.getNativeController(entityID));
+}
